Run mod_websh in your Apache
============================

1. Add the lines from ./conf/httpd.conf to your Apache httpd.conf file.
   (Make sure the paths of LoadModule and WebshConfig point to
   the correct locations)

2. Adapt the DocumentRoot config in your Apache httpd.conf file to
   point to ./htdocs or copy the file from ./htdocs to your preferred
   document root

3. Check ./conf/websh.conf. configure has already filled in webshroot
   and the system encoding, so normally there is nothing to do here.

4. Start Apache and access the demo page /index.html


Where this is installed, and what "make install" touches
=======================================================

Configuration and demo material go to

	<prefix>/share/websh<major>.<minor>/     e.g. share/websh3.7

deliberately without the patch level: WebshConfig in your Apache
configuration keeps pointing at the same file across 3.7.x updates.
The code itself stays fully versioned (lib/websh<full>, bin/websh<full>,
mod_websh<full>.so) -- the Tcl package version and the library name the
module was linked against are part of the contract.

Since that directory holds the file Apache actually reads, "make install"
does not overwrite it:

	conf/websh.conf.dist   always written -- the fresh delivery, to
	                       look up and to diff against
	conf/websh.conf        only created when it does not exist yet;
	                       an existing one is kept, and a difference
	                       to the new delivery is reported
	htdocs/, README        overwritten (demo material)

The system encoding of the shipped websh.conf is chosen at configure time:

	--with-system-encoding=NAME   default utf-8; the name is checked
	                              against the Tcl you build against,
	                              so a typo fails configure instead of
	                              the Apache start
	--without-system-encoding     leave the line out; the encoding then
	                              comes from the locale of the Apache
	                              process


Documentation
=============

For Websh documentation, please refer to http://tcl.apache.org/websh


Files
=====

- Apache module for Apache 1.3 or Apache2 (needs recompile for a 
  different Apache version):
	mod_websh.so            (Unix symbolic link)
	mod_websh<version>.so   (Unix)
	mod_websh.so            (Windows)
	mod_websh<version>.so   (Windows)

- Websh binary for commandline and scripts w/o Apache:
	websh                   (Unix symbolic link)
	websh<version>          (Unix)
	websh.exe               (Windows)
	websh<version>.exe      (Windows)

- Tcl extension (loaded by Websh and mod_websh.so and loadable into 
  a plain Tclsh):
	libwebsh.so             (Unix symbolic link)
	libwebsh<version>.so    (Unix)
	websh.dll               (Windows)
	websh<version>.dll      (Windows)

Note
====

To run the Apache module, modules/mod_websh.so (or 
mod_websh<version>.so respectively), libwebsh.so (or
libwebsh<version>.so respectively) for Unix or websh.dll (or 
websh<version>.dll) for Windows, and the Tcl installation is needed.
